WEBVTT

00:00.561 --> 00:03.849
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.949 --> 00:07.017
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.052 --> 00:10.754
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.789 --> 00:13.757
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.792 --> 00:17.127
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.162 --> 00:20.597
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.632 --> 00:21.965
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.000 --> 00:23.967
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.002 --> 00:25.054
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.557 --> 00:35.378
We now return to Wes Anderson's

00:35.414 --> 00:38.482
<i>Pan Up, Pan Down,
French Song, The End.</i>

00:41.854 --> 00:44.187
♪ Viens, suis-moi ♪

00:44.223 --> 00:45.989
♪ Je connais une route... ♪

00:46.024 --> 00:47.891
Wow, that was amazing, I think!

00:47.926 --> 00:49.626
All right, everyone,

00:49.661 --> 00:51.294
it's time to open up
our bank statements.

00:51.330 --> 00:53.663
Let's gather
'round for prayer.

00:53.699 --> 00:55.966
Hey, God, it's the Griffins.

00:56.001 --> 00:57.667
Again, we're very sorry

00:57.703 --> 00:59.136
we cyber-bullied
that girl to death.

00:59.171 --> 01:01.004
But we still want a snowmobile.

01:01.039 --> 01:02.572
Today, though,
please let there be money

01:02.608 --> 01:03.907
in our bank account.

01:03.942 --> 01:05.509
Amen. Amen.
Amen. Amen.

01:06.745 --> 01:08.044
Damn it.
It didn't work.

01:08.080 --> 01:09.579
We're still poor.

01:09.615 --> 01:12.249
Peter, every month our savings
get smaller and smaller.

01:12.284 --> 01:14.084
We really gotta
figure out a better way

01:14.119 --> 01:15.519
to budget for this
family's future.

01:15.554 --> 01:16.753
Bitcoin.

01:16.789 --> 01:18.021
What?
I don't know.

01:18.056 --> 01:19.422
This is serious.

01:19.458 --> 01:21.358
We need to think
about our kids' education.

01:21.393 --> 01:24.161
Of course, it's already too late
for Meg to go to college.

01:24.196 --> 01:26.530
And Chris is too dumb
to get in anywhere.

01:26.565 --> 01:27.731
Yay!

01:27.766 --> 01:29.032
No, Chris.
Not yay.

01:29.067 --> 01:31.067
But there's still
time for Stewie.

01:31.103 --> 01:33.236
Let's sit down later
and see if we can figure out

01:33.272 --> 01:35.038
a plan to get our
finances in order.

01:35.073 --> 01:36.439
Eh, don't worry
about it, Lois.

01:36.475 --> 01:38.208
I will always provide
for the family.

01:38.243 --> 01:40.110
Even if I have to
shoot our dinner.

01:43.649 --> 01:45.882
This will look great
in my study.

01:45.918 --> 01:47.684
I'm a hunter,

01:47.719 --> 01:49.953
but I'm a silly hunter.

01:58.664 --> 02:00.063
Hey, don't fill up on that.

02:00.098 --> 02:01.531
We got breakfast coming.

02:01.567 --> 02:03.867
Hey, Peter, I think
I figured out one way

02:03.902 --> 02:05.635
we can save money
for Stewie's college.

02:05.671 --> 02:08.371
If we bundle our cable
and Internet together,

02:08.407 --> 02:10.707
we can save
$14 a month.

02:10.742 --> 02:13.076
No! Bundling is
a sign of defeat!

02:13.111 --> 02:14.911
Plus, I figured out
something better.

02:14.947 --> 02:17.214
A metal detector.
What?

02:17.249 --> 02:19.316
Yeah, it combines two of
America's greatest resources:

02:19.351 --> 02:20.584
garbage and luck.

02:20.619 --> 02:21.818
That's stupid,
Peter.

02:21.854 --> 02:23.386
Ah, you're just
saying that

02:23.422 --> 02:25.155
because the battery it uses
causes bladder cancer.

02:25.190 --> 02:26.556
Well, then, I'm off.

02:26.592 --> 02:28.558
I shall be at the beach
looking for valuables

02:28.594 --> 02:30.460
and occasionally using
a doorless bathroom.

02:30.495 --> 02:31.962
Good day, madam.

02:35.901 --> 02:39.035
<i>We now return to
The Awkward Stepdad Show.</i>

02:39.071 --> 02:41.671
Man, your mom's
a real groaner.

02:41.707 --> 02:43.440
Do you hear that
in your room?

02:43.475 --> 02:46.243
Hey, Dad,
where are you going?

02:46.278 --> 02:48.378
Well, Meg, now that
I'm a metal detector guy,

02:48.413 --> 02:50.947
I gotta start eating breakfast
at on-the-sand cafes,

02:50.983 --> 02:52.582
where I will
judge tourists

02:52.618 --> 02:54.618
as my skin browns
and hardens.

02:54.653 --> 02:56.419
Stop throwin' your kid's diapers

02:56.455 --> 02:58.889
in the trash
with all the soda cans!

03:02.561 --> 03:05.061
Hey, Lois, check out what
I found with my metal detector.

03:06.732 --> 03:09.032
Are those... are
those Purple Hearts?

03:09.067 --> 03:10.907
Yeah, some idiot buried,
like, a hundred of 'em

03:10.936 --> 03:12.602
in this big lawn
under these bone cages.

03:12.638 --> 03:14.104
Peter!

03:14.139 --> 03:16.706
I think you desecrated
a military graveyard!

03:16.742 --> 03:18.375
Hey, guys, like four jeeps

03:18.410 --> 03:19.943
just drove up
onto our front yard.

03:19.978 --> 03:21.444
They must be here
for the medals!

03:21.480 --> 03:23.380
Maybe. Or it could be
because of my

03:23.415 --> 03:25.749
"I'm Gonna Barf
on the White House" blog.

03:32.324 --> 03:35.091
Ah, sweet!

03:35.127 --> 03:36.927
Huh.

03:36.962 --> 03:39.482
Wonder what happens if I turn it
on and point 'em at each other.

03:42.467 --> 03:43.900
Oh, my God!

03:43.936 --> 03:46.503
Did you also call
into a talk show

03:46.538 --> 03:49.239
without turning down
your radio first?

03:52.311 --> 03:54.144
Jackpot.

03:54.179 --> 03:55.679
Wow, an iPad!

03:55.714 --> 03:56.947
This thing finds
everything!

03:56.982 --> 03:58.949
Engagement ring!

03:58.984 --> 04:00.784
Family locket!

04:00.819 --> 04:02.786
Sunglasses that are an upgrade

04:02.821 --> 04:05.121
- over my current pair!
- There he is!

04:05.157 --> 04:07.958
There's the guy who's been
stealing everyone's stuff!

04:07.993 --> 04:10.527
Don't yell at me,
I'm very sunburned!

04:10.562 --> 04:13.964
Go, crappy car, go!

04:17.202 --> 04:20.437
Peter, did you rob
a bunch of people

04:20.472 --> 04:22.172
on the beach
with your metal detector?

04:22.207 --> 04:23.773
Well, that's only
half the story.

04:23.809 --> 04:25.842
I also hooted at a lady
who was breastfeeding.

04:25.877 --> 04:28.211
I want you to get rid of
that metal detector.

04:28.246 --> 04:30.013
All you're doing is
getting into trouble

04:30.048 --> 04:32.015
and digging up junk
when we really need

04:32.050 --> 04:33.683
to be saving
for Stewie's college.

04:33.719 --> 04:35.352
Tomorrow we are
going to the mall

04:35.387 --> 04:37.153
and returning that
thing to the store.

04:37.189 --> 04:38.822
Okay, fine.

04:38.857 --> 04:41.291
But you should know, the day
I bought this metal detector

04:41.326 --> 04:43.693
was the happiest
day of my life.

04:43.729 --> 04:46.663
Well, obviously,
the second happiest.

04:46.698 --> 04:50.667
♪ Now we gonna do this thing
a little different tonight ♪

04:52.371 --> 04:57.507
♪ You gonna come over,
pick me up in your ride ♪

04:57.542 --> 05:00.010
Oh, my God, I wasn't even
supposed to be here.

05:00.045 --> 05:02.145
I passed out at the Tom Petty
concert last night

05:02.180 --> 05:03.480
and just stayed.

05:03.515 --> 05:06.216
♪ You're gonna open my door ♪

05:06.251 --> 05:09.719
♪ And I'm gonna reach over
and open yours ♪

05:09.755 --> 05:12.889
♪ Gonna pay for dinner,
take me to see a movie ♪

05:12.924 --> 05:16.092
♪ And whisper in my ear how bad
you really want to do me... ♪

05:16.128 --> 05:18.028
Please, go slow.

05:18.063 --> 05:19.963
I have IBS.

05:24.536 --> 05:26.269
Well, I'm glad
the store was willing

05:26.304 --> 05:27.837
to take that
metal detector back.

05:27.873 --> 05:29.239
All right, let's go
to the food court.

05:29.274 --> 05:31.074
I love eating
Panda Express

05:31.109 --> 05:33.176
while squeezin' our purchases
between our knees

05:33.211 --> 05:34.577
'cause someone
might grab 'em.

05:34.613 --> 05:36.679
God, the mall sucks,
doesn't it, kids?

05:36.715 --> 05:38.515
If I had a credit card,
I'd shop online.

05:38.550 --> 05:40.050
Oh, hey, Bonnie.

05:40.085 --> 05:41.451
What are you guys
doing here?

05:41.486 --> 05:42.786
Oh, hey, Lois.

05:42.821 --> 05:44.788
We saw an ad
looking for a toddler

05:44.823 --> 05:46.589
to appear in a peanut
butter commercial

05:46.625 --> 05:48.925
and we thought
we'd bring Susie.

05:48.960 --> 05:51.594
Joe, are you wearing a corsage?
Yeah.

05:51.630 --> 05:53.630
You can get a really good deal
on them after prom season.

05:53.665 --> 05:54.898
They're for girls, Joe.

05:54.933 --> 05:56.433
Hey, Peter,

05:56.468 --> 05:59.369
why don't you let me do me,
and you do you, okay?

05:59.404 --> 06:01.071
Peanut butter commercial, huh?

06:01.106 --> 06:02.739
Hey, Bri, maybe
you should audition.

06:02.774 --> 06:04.941
You know, because of that
one time you got in the trash

06:04.976 --> 06:06.943
and ate a whole jar of
recalled peanut butter?

06:06.978 --> 06:08.578
It wasn't peanut butter.

06:08.613 --> 06:10.380
It was that pre-mixed peanut
butter and jelly thing.

06:10.415 --> 06:11.915
Oh, Mom bought that?

06:11.950 --> 06:14.617
That's what the scab kid
at school always has!

06:14.653 --> 06:16.386
That was really great, Jake.

06:16.421 --> 06:17.620
Really, really great.

06:17.656 --> 06:19.322
Your face is upside-down,

06:19.357 --> 06:21.558
so we're not gonna pick you,
but thanks for coming.

06:21.593 --> 06:23.226
Hey. Hey.
This is you.

06:23.261 --> 06:24.461
"I'm Brian.

06:24.496 --> 06:26.229
"I like garbage
peanut butter,

06:26.264 --> 06:29.099
and I wear my 'I Voted' sticker
for a week and a half."

06:29.134 --> 06:30.333
Num-num-num-num-num-
num-num-num-num!

06:31.636 --> 06:33.103
I'm sorry, we're looking for

06:33.138 --> 06:34.504
more of a
"Num-num-num-num-num-num-num."

06:34.539 --> 06:37.140
Bob, look over there!

06:37.175 --> 06:39.476
Num-num-num-num-num-num-num-num-
num-num-num-num-num!

06:41.255 --> 06:42.488
Whose kid is that?

06:42.523 --> 06:44.323
Oh, that's our son, Stewie.

06:44.359 --> 06:45.758
He's adorable!

06:45.793 --> 06:47.693
And exactly what
we're looking for!

06:47.729 --> 06:51.430
Congratulations, your son
is the new peanut butter kid!

06:51.466 --> 06:53.432
My God, I don't believe it!

06:53.468 --> 06:55.067
That's so cool!

06:55.103 --> 06:57.103
Hey, what's Dad doing
over there with Chris?

06:57.138 --> 07:00.039
Oh, he's telling him that he's
no longer his favorite son.

07:03.411 --> 07:05.077
No!

07:05.113 --> 07:07.880
No, Daddy!

07:07.915 --> 07:11.250
Daddy!

07:11.285 --> 07:13.185
Daddy...

07:20.228 --> 07:22.194
I didn't even tell him.

07:22.230 --> 07:24.063
He just does not
like to be touched.

07:29.144 --> 07:30.911
Thanks for coming
to the viewing party

07:30.946 --> 07:33.013
for Stewie's commercial,
everybody.

07:33.048 --> 07:35.916
<i>We're sorry that it's
airing during 2 Broke Girls,</i>

07:35.951 --> 07:37.818
but we have no
control over that.

07:37.853 --> 07:39.853
Thanks for coming to
my big night, Brian.

07:39.889 --> 07:42.823
I see you got all dressed up
in your exposed wiener.

07:42.858 --> 07:44.958
Quiet, everybody!
Here it comes!

07:46.996 --> 07:48.962
Welcome home, honey!

07:49.965 --> 07:51.498
There's my family!

07:51.534 --> 07:53.534
H-Hey, wait,
where's the baby?

07:53.569 --> 07:56.103
Well, he likes
his hero dad,

07:56.138 --> 07:58.639
but he loves
Scooter's Peanut Butter.

07:58.674 --> 08:02.276
Num-num-num-num-num-num-num-num-
num-num-num-num-num-num-num!

08:02.311 --> 08:03.844
<i>Scooter's Peanut Butter.</i>

08:03.879 --> 08:05.712
<i>So good, your baby
will want to eat it</i>

08:05.748 --> 08:07.814
<i>in an airport terminal
bathroom.</i>

08:09.318 --> 08:11.552
He's a baby
who did a baby thing.

08:11.587 --> 08:13.186
Let's all calm down
a little.

08:13.222 --> 08:15.489
Wow, I can't believe
Stewie's a commercial star.

08:15.524 --> 08:17.391
We haven't had a
celebrity in the family

08:17.426 --> 08:19.893
since my great-aunt,
Queen of Burlesque Griffin.

08:21.196 --> 08:22.729
♪ Cheesy jokes ♪

08:22.765 --> 08:25.566
♪ And ugly broads ♪

08:25.601 --> 08:27.534
♪ Way back when ♪

08:27.570 --> 08:29.836
♪ They had no porn ♪

08:29.872 --> 08:31.338
♪ Just scarves ♪

08:31.373 --> 08:32.739
♪ Fans ♪

08:32.775 --> 08:34.074
♪ Fat ♪

08:34.109 --> 08:35.342
♪ Gross ♪

08:35.377 --> 08:37.744
♪ A terrible time ♪

08:37.780 --> 08:40.547
♪ For your penis to live in... ♪

08:44.920 --> 08:47.688
Bill. Bill. Bill.

08:47.723 --> 08:50.324
Weird magazine about
our town that's just ads.

08:50.359 --> 08:52.526
Hmm, this one's for Stewie.

08:52.561 --> 08:55.228
Whoa, a check for $2,000?

08:55.264 --> 08:56.897
Let me see that.

08:56.932 --> 08:59.700
It's a royalty check
from Stewie's commercial.

08:59.735 --> 09:02.102
Apparently, he gets paid
every time it airs.

09:02.137 --> 09:03.737
This is great.

09:03.772 --> 09:06.039
We can put it right into
Stewie's college fund.

09:06.075 --> 09:08.008
Yeah, yeah,
but, you know,

09:08.043 --> 09:09.910
maybe we should keep
a little bit out to celebrate.

09:09.945 --> 09:11.678
I mean, I ain't
done nothin' fancy

09:11.714 --> 09:13.680
since I bought
those rich guy socks.

09:13.716 --> 09:15.349
Ah, there.

09:15.384 --> 09:18.552
I'm ready to get caught
cheating with my secretary.

09:18.587 --> 09:21.121
♪ ♪

09:23.826 --> 09:25.392
Welcome, folks.

09:25.427 --> 09:27.427
Would you like flat
or sparkling water to start?

09:27.463 --> 09:28.695
Garden hose
will be fine.

09:28.731 --> 09:31.031
We prefer it to be hot
and then metal-y.

09:31.066 --> 09:32.466
Actually, Peter,

09:32.501 --> 09:34.401
let's go for the
sparkling water.

09:34.436 --> 09:35.936
I mean, we are
celebrating

09:35.971 --> 09:38.572
our little commercial
star and his big payday.

09:38.607 --> 09:40.807
Oh, I don't care
about that, ma'am.

09:40.843 --> 09:42.476
You know, this is
a nice dinner and all,

09:42.511 --> 09:44.311
but I thought you guys
were going to save

09:44.346 --> 09:46.313
this commercial money
for Stewie's college fund.

09:46.348 --> 09:48.482
We are saving it, Brian.

09:48.517 --> 09:50.250
This is just
a little celebration.

09:50.285 --> 09:52.419
The rest of it is going
right in the bank.

09:52.454 --> 09:53.954
Yeah, and besides,
it's been a while

09:53.989 --> 09:55.889
since we ate at a place
where if you ask for ketchup,

09:55.924 --> 09:57.124
they look at you
like you're dirt.

09:57.159 --> 09:58.792
You know, Stewie
actually got a call

09:58.827 --> 10:00.227
for another
commercial tomorrow.

10:00.262 --> 10:01.928
Who knows?

10:01.964 --> 10:04.097
This could be the beginning
of a nice career for him.

10:04.133 --> 10:05.599
You sure about this, Lois?

10:05.634 --> 10:07.434
I mean... I mean,
the world of child acting

10:07.469 --> 10:09.336
can be a pretty bad
environment for a kid.

10:09.371 --> 10:11.338
Maybe we should just
let Stewie's childhood

10:11.373 --> 10:12.806
be about being a child.

10:12.841 --> 10:14.808
Wasn't your kid an actor,
you jagoff?

10:14.843 --> 10:16.510
Didn't your father
hate your guts and die?

10:16.545 --> 10:17.778
Whoa!

10:17.813 --> 10:19.279
Bring a gun to a knife fight.

10:19.314 --> 10:20.681
Look, I-I'm sorry,
I'm sorry.

10:20.716 --> 10:22.249
All I'm saying is,

10:22.284 --> 10:24.117
just try to keep Stewie's
best interests in mind.

10:24.153 --> 10:25.519
Relax, Brian.

10:25.554 --> 10:27.020
Stewie's fine.
I mean, look at him.

10:27.056 --> 10:29.156
He's happier than
a sunny-side-up egg.

10:29.191 --> 10:31.158
What a great way
to start the day.

10:31.193 --> 10:33.994
What a pan, what a grill.

10:34.029 --> 10:35.829
Oh no, I'm at Denny's.

10:35.864 --> 10:38.265
Hey, I'm a drug addict
and it's midnight--

10:38.300 --> 10:39.666
where's my breakfast?!

10:39.702 --> 10:41.501
Help, he's only
gonna eat the toast

10:41.537 --> 10:43.537
and put a cigarette out on me.

10:47.009 --> 10:49.376
Okay, Stewie, you booked
the last commercial

10:49.411 --> 10:52.212
without even trying, so this
one should be a piece of cake.

10:54.483 --> 10:57.851
Oh, I guess there are other
people auditioning, too.

10:57.886 --> 11:01.288
Oh, is your child up for the
cough syrup commercial, too?

11:01.323 --> 11:03.290
You'd have no way
of knowing this,

11:03.325 --> 11:05.292
but the moms tend
to dress up.

11:05.327 --> 11:07.294
Oh, thank you.

11:07.329 --> 11:09.129
And you'd have
no way of knowing

11:09.164 --> 11:10.964
that my son is the
Scooter's Peanut Butter Kid.

11:10.999 --> 11:12.966
That's cute.

11:13.001 --> 11:16.369
<i>My son had a gun waved in
his face in a Dexter episode.</i>

11:16.405 --> 11:18.805
Are you guys talking
about your kids?

11:18.841 --> 11:21.541
My daughter is the American
Apparel slut baby.

11:22.811 --> 11:26.480
<i>My son got crapped on
in the last Jackass movie.</i>

11:26.515 --> 11:29.483
God, everyone here
is so talented.

11:29.518 --> 11:31.885
Hi, everybody, we're
a little crunched for time,

11:31.920 --> 11:33.720
so we're gonna have
to audition people

11:33.756 --> 11:35.055
right here
in the hallway.

11:35.090 --> 11:36.490
You, do something
exceptional.

11:36.525 --> 11:38.391
Uh, okay.

11:43.866 --> 11:45.665
Ow! Ow.

11:45.701 --> 11:47.067
Oh, my grundle.

11:47.102 --> 11:48.068
It's bruised.

11:48.103 --> 11:49.503
It's bruised bad.

11:49.538 --> 11:51.338
Oh, okay, I'm out, I'm out.

11:51.373 --> 11:52.739
Tappin' out.

11:52.775 --> 11:55.175
Well, that was
a disaster.

11:55.210 --> 11:57.177
It was humiliating
is what it was.

11:57.212 --> 11:58.578
That woman just smiled

11:58.614 --> 12:00.580
when Stewie banged
his balls on the floor.

12:00.616 --> 12:02.582
A damn disaster.

12:02.618 --> 12:04.584
Num-num-num-num-num-
num-num-num-num?

12:04.620 --> 12:06.353
Shut up,
that's over!

12:06.388 --> 12:07.554
Did you see those other kids?

12:07.589 --> 12:08.755
They were amazing.

12:08.791 --> 12:10.190
One of them was texting

12:10.225 --> 12:12.025
<i>with the funny-dumb kid
from Modern Family.</i>

12:12.060 --> 12:13.593
I want to text with that kid.

12:13.629 --> 12:15.428
Holy Christmas, there were
a lot of hot moms

12:15.464 --> 12:17.097
in yoga pants in there though.

12:17.132 --> 12:19.933
Dear me, they're really
disappointed in me, Rupert.

12:19.968 --> 12:21.768
I haven't seen
the fat man this upset

12:21.804 --> 12:23.637
since he went
to the 9/11 museum.

12:23.672 --> 12:25.639
Lois made us do this,

12:25.674 --> 12:28.742
but I wanted to go to the
Central Park merry-go-round.

12:28.777 --> 12:31.111
We had time to do both!

12:35.584 --> 12:38.118
What the hell?

12:40.055 --> 12:42.055
♪ ♪

12:50.465 --> 12:52.432
Okay, that's great, that's
great, that's great.

12:52.467 --> 12:54.267
Just one question,
Stewie--

12:54.303 --> 12:56.670
do you get pleasure out of
humiliating your family?

12:56.705 --> 12:59.105
Yeah, is there some kind
of sick joy in it?

12:59.141 --> 13:00.941
Why can't he just
be Pierce Brosnan?

13:00.976 --> 13:02.242
Pierce Brosnan
would've got this.

13:02.277 --> 13:03.243
In a heartbeat!

13:03.278 --> 13:04.511
It's 3:00
in the morning.

13:04.546 --> 13:05.946
What the hell
are you guys doing?

13:05.981 --> 13:08.148
What does it look like?
We're practicing.

13:08.183 --> 13:09.783
Stewie has another
audition tomorrow,

13:09.818 --> 13:11.685
and we're not gonna be
embarrassed like we were today.

13:11.720 --> 13:14.120
See, this is the kind
of thing I was talking about.

13:14.156 --> 13:15.856
And look at him,
he can barely stand up.

13:15.891 --> 13:18.792
That's why I made this--
I call it "8 Hour Energy."

13:18.827 --> 13:21.428
It's one part 5-Hour Energy,
and the other three hours are

13:21.463 --> 13:23.029
espresso, Scotts
Turf Builder,

13:23.065 --> 13:26.032
and a tiny, tiny super-small
amount of cocaine.

13:26.068 --> 13:27.500
Just a little bit.

13:27.536 --> 13:29.936
I can't stress the
littleness of it enough.

13:31.807 --> 13:34.174
Whoa, mama,
there's a kick like a mule!

13:34.209 --> 13:37.177
♪ Who will buy
this wonderful morning ♪

13:37.212 --> 13:39.613
♪ Such a sky
you never did see. ♪

13:39.648 --> 13:41.448
There he is,
there's the magic.

13:41.483 --> 13:42.849
Peter, you're giving
your baby drugs

13:42.885 --> 13:44.284
to improve
his acting career?

13:44.319 --> 13:45.685
Oh, he's fine
with it.

13:45.721 --> 13:46.686
Stewie, if you're
fine with it,

13:46.722 --> 13:49.122
bleed from the nose.

13:49.157 --> 13:51.024
I think that's
pretty close.

13:59.304 --> 14:01.671
All right, Stewie, now remember
what we practiced last night.

14:01.706 --> 14:03.673
And here's a trick
to keep that confidence up.

14:03.708 --> 14:05.108
You go in that room

14:05.143 --> 14:07.510
and imagine everyone in it
wants you sexually.

14:07.545 --> 14:10.513
I'm doing it right now,
and I feel powerful.

14:10.548 --> 14:11.948
Okay.

14:11.983 --> 14:13.950
And don't forget--
if you screw this up,

14:13.985 --> 14:15.910
Mommy's gonna kill
all of your toys.

14:15.934 --> 14:16.821
Okay.

14:16.821 --> 14:19.288
All right, now I'm gonna go
psych out these other kids.

14:19.324 --> 14:20.690
Hey, little guy.

14:20.725 --> 14:21.691
Nervous?

14:21.726 --> 14:23.126
Sure you are.

14:23.161 --> 14:24.527
Here's something
that might help you.

14:26.564 --> 14:28.197
Hey, little guy.

14:28.233 --> 14:29.399
Stewie Griffin?

14:29.434 --> 14:30.633
Oh, right here.

14:30.668 --> 14:32.035
Peter, he
needs a boost.

14:32.070 --> 14:33.770
Give him some of
the acting soup.

14:36.207 --> 14:38.608
I want to say curse words!

14:40.745 --> 14:43.146
Okay, Stewie, you're just
gonna drink this juice,

14:43.181 --> 14:45.982
then say, "Mmm,"
and rub your belly.

14:46.017 --> 14:47.017
Yeah, yeah,
you got it.

14:48.887 --> 14:50.219
Yeah! Bye, juice!

14:50.255 --> 14:51.654
That was amazing.

14:51.689 --> 14:53.056
I've got goosebumps.

14:53.091 --> 14:54.657
I want him
sexually.

14:54.692 --> 14:57.193
Well, Mom, Dad,

14:57.228 --> 14:59.495
I think we've got our
new orange juice boy.

14:59.531 --> 15:01.497
Does this guy really
think we're his parents?

15:01.533 --> 15:02.899
Stewie got the part?!

15:02.934 --> 15:04.333
Yes!

15:04.369 --> 15:07.370
That is how
you do it.

15:12.710 --> 15:14.277
Oh, hey, Brian.
What's going on?

15:14.312 --> 15:15.278
Where's the fridge?

15:15.313 --> 15:16.679
Oh, we got a new one.

15:16.714 --> 15:18.514
Stewie booked that
orange juice commercial,

15:18.550 --> 15:20.917
so we thought we'd make a few
upgrades around the house.

15:20.952 --> 15:23.920
Yeah, I even bought an awesome
voice-activated 3-D printer.

15:23.955 --> 15:25.855
Why the hell do you
need a 3-D printer?

15:25.890 --> 15:27.256
Print coyote.

15:32.730 --> 15:34.097
Hey, what,
hey, no, no, no!

15:34.132 --> 15:36.065
Heel, heel, heel!

15:36.101 --> 15:37.300
I can't make him
attack you, Brian,

15:37.335 --> 15:38.534
but if I keep
printing them,

15:38.570 --> 15:40.069
eventually one will
go after you.

15:40.105 --> 15:41.904
That money is supposed to
be for Stewie's college.

15:41.940 --> 15:44.740
He's an actor, you idiot--
he doesn't need college.

15:44.776 --> 15:47.577
Look, I-I just don't think any
of this is good for Stewie.

15:47.612 --> 15:48.978
It's great for Stewie.

15:49.013 --> 15:50.213
He's becoming a star.

15:50.248 --> 15:52.215
That's right.

15:52.250 --> 15:55.084
Man, this must be what it's like
to be Anne Hathaway's parents.

15:56.654 --> 15:58.454
Oh, that's Anne's car.

15:58.490 --> 15:59.922
Ugh.

16:02.961 --> 16:04.427
Hey, Stewie, can
I talk to you?

16:04.462 --> 16:05.928
What are you doing?

16:05.964 --> 16:07.597
I don't know.

16:07.632 --> 16:10.933
Mom and Dad just, uh, stuck
a book on my head and-and left.

16:10.969 --> 16:12.935
Stewie, look at you,
you're a wreck.

16:12.971 --> 16:15.338
And for what? So Peter and Lois
can spend the money you earned

16:15.373 --> 16:16.772
on crap they
don't even need?

16:16.808 --> 16:19.175
Uh, I'm not supposed
to use my voice

16:19.210 --> 16:21.010
for non-paying
stuff, Brian.

16:21.045 --> 16:22.845
This is insane--
you've got to stop.

16:22.881 --> 16:25.681
Ugh, stop worrying,
I'm fine.

16:25.717 --> 16:28.117
And besides, the fat man
knows what he's doing.

16:28.153 --> 16:29.519
No, he doesn't,
he's an idiot.

16:29.554 --> 16:30.994
Remember? He couldn't
even figure out

16:31.022 --> 16:32.989
how to use a hotel
business center.

16:33.024 --> 16:35.825
So what business
are you in?

16:35.860 --> 16:37.827
Oh, I'm just here to look
at other people's e-mails

16:37.862 --> 16:40.263
who haven't logged out.
And how's business?

16:40.298 --> 16:43.266
Well, I've left some pretty wild
replies on a bunch of Evites.

16:43.301 --> 16:46.269
Look at this-- I'm
bringing 53 guests.

16:46.304 --> 16:49.872
You're the coolest guy I've ever
met in one of these things.

16:55.013 --> 16:56.379
Oh, hey.

16:56.414 --> 16:58.214
You caught me
pigging out.

16:58.249 --> 17:00.216
I'm dipping this celery
stalk into some lemon water.

17:00.251 --> 17:02.051
But don't freak out.

17:02.086 --> 17:04.053
I'm just gonna smell it and
then throw it in the trash.

17:04.088 --> 17:05.888
Stewie, this has
gotten out of control.

17:05.924 --> 17:07.723
If you're gonna
continue on this path,

17:07.759 --> 17:09.559
you need to know
what your future holds.

17:09.594 --> 17:11.994
Being a child actor
almost never ends well.

17:12.030 --> 17:13.829
<i>You remember that kid
from A Christmas Story</i>

17:13.865 --> 17:15.231
who got his tongue
stuck to that pole?

17:15.266 --> 17:16.666
Yeah, whatever
happened to him?

17:16.701 --> 17:18.067
I'll tell you
what happened to him.

17:18.102 --> 17:19.502
He did porn.

17:19.537 --> 17:21.337
<i>Boner from Growing Pains? Dead.</i>

17:21.372 --> 17:23.339
<i>Screech from
Saved by the Bell? Porn.</i>

17:23.374 --> 17:24.740
Corey Haim? Dead.

17:24.776 --> 17:27.076
Dana Plato? Porn, then dead.

17:27.111 --> 17:28.878
Oh, no, this is horrible.

17:28.913 --> 17:31.314
You see, Stewie, there are
tons of actors like this.

17:31.349 --> 17:33.316
They all started out
just like you,

17:33.351 --> 17:34.717
but eventually
they were destroyed

17:34.752 --> 17:36.552
by their parents'
greed, drugs

17:36.588 --> 17:37.987
or perverted
Hollywood directors.

17:38.022 --> 17:39.388
Oh, like Bryan Singer.

17:39.424 --> 17:42.225
Exactly. The point is
it's a dark path.

17:42.260 --> 17:44.660
My God, I had no idea
it could be so bad.

17:44.696 --> 17:46.495
Brian, I don't want
to act anymore.

17:46.531 --> 17:49.498
Good. Now we just got to make
Peter and Lois understand.

17:49.534 --> 17:51.500
Yes, well, if they want
to make me into a monster

17:51.536 --> 17:54.337
like those people, we'll
give 'em a monster.

17:54.372 --> 17:56.539
Like when Godzilla
attacked Haiti.

18:00.712 --> 18:02.712
Oh, my God.

18:13.424 --> 18:15.391
Peter, did you
get my text?

18:15.426 --> 18:17.793
No, hold on.

18:17.829 --> 18:19.795
No, I don't know
what he's doing here.

18:19.831 --> 18:22.231
Okay, Stewie, when Barbara
hands you that orange juice,

18:22.267 --> 18:24.066
you're gonna drink it
and smile.

18:24.102 --> 18:26.469
And really show us that
energy from your audition.

18:26.504 --> 18:28.471
H-Hold on a second,
he's got a smudge on his face.

18:28.506 --> 18:30.039
Let me just take care
of that for you guys.

18:30.074 --> 18:31.440
Here, drink this.

18:31.476 --> 18:32.875
I threw a little Molly
in there, too,

18:32.910 --> 18:34.310
so we'll go out
clubbing afterwards.

18:38.983 --> 18:40.383
Hey, you want this?

18:40.418 --> 18:41.784
Sure, I'll
drink anything.

18:41.819 --> 18:43.419
All right, action!

18:43.454 --> 18:46.822
As a mom, I want my kids
to start their day right.

18:46.858 --> 18:48.824
And there's no better way
than with a glass

18:48.860 --> 18:51.260
of fresh-squeezed
Sunnydale Orange Juice.

18:51.296 --> 18:52.662
Isn't that right,
sweetie?

18:52.697 --> 18:54.497
Shut your hole, bitch!

18:54.532 --> 18:56.499
I'll tell you what I want
fresh-squeezed-- these.

18:57.969 --> 18:59.335
What the hell's
he doing?

18:59.370 --> 19:00.803
He's blowing this.

19:00.838 --> 19:04.240
Oh, here's what I think
of this orange juice.

19:07.278 --> 19:10.246
I-I can't... I can't go right
now with everybody watching.

19:10.281 --> 19:13.949
But-but I presume you understand
the disrespect I intended.

19:13.985 --> 19:15.951
Oh, my God, he's
having a meltdown.

19:15.987 --> 19:17.353
You don't suppose this
has anything to do

19:17.388 --> 19:19.355
with the sleep deprivation
and narcotics?

19:19.390 --> 19:22.191
Oh, Peter, what have
we been thinking?

19:22.226 --> 19:25.194
It's us-- we're the ones
who turned him into this.

19:25.229 --> 19:27.496
Get this kid out of here!
He's fired.

19:28.533 --> 19:29.932
Well done.

19:29.967 --> 19:31.334
Not a bad performance.

19:31.369 --> 19:32.768
Thank you, Brian, I...

19:32.804 --> 19:33.769
Uh, there's the poop.

19:33.805 --> 19:34.770
Right now.

19:34.806 --> 19:36.172
Oh, Stewie.

19:36.207 --> 19:38.174
Mommy and Daddy
are so sorry.

19:38.209 --> 19:41.010
I-I guess we just got
too caught up in your success

19:41.045 --> 19:43.012
and forgot that you're
just a baby.

19:43.047 --> 19:44.447
You were
right, Brian.

19:44.482 --> 19:46.849
I guess we pushed Stewie
a little too hard.

19:46.884 --> 19:48.851
Well, the good news is
that now he can go back

19:48.886 --> 19:50.853
to being a regular kid.

19:50.888 --> 19:52.855
♪ ♪

19:52.890 --> 19:54.857
Why are you winking at
our baby, you creep?

19:54.892 --> 19:56.659
God, that's weird.

19:56.694 --> 19:58.527
I don't want to ever
see that happen again.

20:02.633 --> 20:05.601
Well, we went a little crazy
there, didn't we, Peter?

20:05.636 --> 20:07.002
But I'm glad we have

20:07.038 --> 20:09.772
our normal, very average,
non-famous baby back.

20:09.807 --> 20:11.607
You know, I was once
a very famous baby.

20:11.642 --> 20:13.209
Were you, Peter?

20:13.244 --> 20:15.444
No, but you see how easy
it is for me to lie to you?

20:15.480 --> 20:17.146
I do it every day.

20:17.181 --> 20:19.548
Anyway, looks like everything
worked out for the best.

20:19.584 --> 20:21.584
You know, Brian, that acting
stuff was a bit much for me,

20:21.619 --> 20:24.220
but I did quite enjoy
the dancing and the cocaine.

20:24.255 --> 20:26.055
Yeah?
Yep.

20:26.090 --> 20:27.890
So you're just gonna be a
dancer and a drug addict?

20:27.925 --> 20:30.326
For a while. I might
crash when I'm 18,

20:30.361 --> 20:32.728
but then I'll just turn
to the Lord and working out.

20:32.764 --> 20:37.266
I'll-I'll just be a 180 degree
different type of insufferable.

20:37.301 --> 20:39.268
I used to need drugs
to feel powerful,

20:39.303 --> 20:41.704
but now my power comes
from my core strength.

20:41.739 --> 20:43.539
And let's look at that
word, "strength."

20:43.574 --> 20:45.541
The "S" stands
for sacrifice.

20:45.576 --> 20:47.343
No gain without
sacrifice.

20:47.378 --> 20:50.513
The "T," of course, stands for
the sufferings of the cross.

20:50.548 --> 20:52.314
The "R"...
You want some cocaine?

20:52.350 --> 20:54.950
Oh, my God, please, yes!
That's all I want all the time!

20:54.974 --> 21:01.474
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru